-- Migration: 0050_dire_maul_route
-- Date:    2026-11-20
-- Purpose: Dire Maul's dungeon route (playerbot_dungeon_routes, map 429) covered the East wing only: 1432 crumbs that looped
--          round the East wing (x -153..308, y -527..-147) and none in the West or North wing, so a tank heading for any West or
--          North boss beyond the path cap had no route to follow (Tendris Warpwood was 627 y from the nearest crumb, King Gordok
--          944 y). The route is rebuilt from the 429 navmesh, one chain per wing from its entrance (the dmeast/dmwest/dmnorth
--          scenario starts), in DireMaulScript.cpp's boss order:
--            seq   0-224  East: Pusillin's spot, Hydrospawn, Lethtendris, Zevrim Thornhoof, Alzzin the Wildshaper
--            seq 225-427  West: the first pylon, Tendris Warpwood, Magister Kalendris, Illyanna Ravenoak, the other four pylons,
--                         Immol'thar, Prince Tortheldrin
--            seq 428-535  North: Guard Mol'dar, Stomper Kreeg, Fengus's Chest, Guard Fengus, Guard Slip'kik, Captain Kromcrush,
--                         Cho'Rush the Observer, King Gordok
--          The West chain goes into the room of each of the five pylons (the crystal generators): Immol'thar's force field drops
--          only when every Arcane Aberration and Mana Remnant within 20 y of each pylon is dead (classic_instance_dire_maul.cpp,
--          TYPE_CRISTAL_EVENT). The North chain passes Fengus's Chest, which holds the Gordok Courtyard Key.
--          A crumb about every 18 y of walked path (536 crumbs, gaps 3-26 y; walked East about 4030 y, West 3610 y, North 1820 y).
--          Every crumb-to-crumb leg is a clean path of at most 8 polygons. Some legs pass a door that is shut until something
--          opens it, as for a player: the Conservatory Door (seq 196-198, Ironbark the Redeemed opens it), the Crescent Key door
--          after Tendris (seq 349-351; its lock also takes a plain open, so the bots open it by hand), Immol'thar's force field
--          (seq 395-399), the doors to Tortheldrin (seq 412-415), the Gordok Courtyard Door (seq 474-476, the Courtyard Key)
--          and the Gordok Inner Door (seq 515-517, the Inner Door Key Guard Mol'dar drops). The wings do not join where these doors are shut; the route follower skips a crumb it cannot
--          reach, so each wing's crumbs only come into play inside that wing.
-- Reverts: yes (the old 1432 rows are in sql/playerbot_shared/playerbot_shared_data.sql).

-- @target: shared

DELETE FROM {SHARED}.playerbot_dungeon_routes WHERE map_id = 429;

